{"uid":"86a98dc81136785a","name":"test_an_uncorroborated_claim_now_backs_off_instead_of_tripping_the_three_strike_guard","fullName":"tests.test_progress_pin_task015#test_an_uncorroborated_claim_now_backs_off_instead_of_tripping_the_three_strike_guard","historyId":"fc1a01e9a7c9d28a8b487ccffc083438","time":{"start":1792072289024,"stop":1792072289144,"duration":120},"description":"Three consecutive `file`-kind claims, none backed by a real tree\n    delta -- uncorroborated every time (task 012's own pinned behaviour),\n    which is EXACTLY what requirement A.5's letter 2 used to call the\n    pre-existing three-strike guard still firing \"exactly as it did before\n    this wave touched anything.\"\n\n    PRD v0.29 #279 cure (task 014's sweep): that is no longer true, and\n    cannot be made true again by any choice of scripted claim shape --\n    #279's `_apply_engine_repoll_backoff` trigger is defined over the\n    SAME signal this scenario is built from (`verdict == \"no_verdict\"`,\n    `corroborated: false`, `deltaSize: 0`, two consecutive times on one\n    task), and it fires BEFORE a third such pass can ever reach the\n    three-strike guard's own counter: pass 2 is the first ordinary\n    witness (old counter -> 1), but pass 2 is ALSO the first of what\n    becomes two consecutive re-polls, so the re-poll that would have been\n    pass 3 instead backs the task off for 600s -- requirement A.3's own\n    \"a re-poll that triggers a backoff neither increments nor resets the\n    approach's stagnation counter\" -- and the counter never reaches 3.\n    task 014's own sweep crashed an xdist worker on this exact node before\n    this cure (the module's own `_worker_sup` built `sup` directly rather\n    than through `tests.conftest.make_supervisor`, leaving the backoff's\n    real `asyncio.sleep(600)` unpatched -- `_patch_sleep_for_this_test()`\n    now closes that, matching `tests/test_repoll_backoff.py`'s own\n    documented reasoning for the same gap).\n\n    What is left to pin, and what this rewrite asserts instead: the claims\n    are still recorded and still uncorroborated every time (task 012's\n    letter, unaffected by #279); the OLD three-strike STAGNATION_MESSAGE\n    never appears (superseded, not merely absent by accident); #279's own\n    backoff fires twice (`consecutiveCount` 2 then 3, since the third\n    scripted call is ALSO a re-poll on the already-once-backed-off task);\n    and the task ends up deferred (`pending`, a `re-poll backoff`\n    `deferredReason`) rather than whatever the pre-#279 guard would have\n    left it as.","descriptionHtml":"<p>Three consecutive <code>file</code>-kind claims, none backed by a real tree<br />\ndelta -- uncorroborated every time (task 012's own pinned behaviour),<br />\nwhich is EXACTLY what requirement A.5's letter 2 used to call the<br />\npre-existing three-strike guard still firing &quot;exactly as it did before<br />\nthis wave touched anything.&quot;</p>\n<pre><code>PRD v0.29 #279 cure (task 014's sweep): that is no longer true, and\ncannot be made true again by any choice of scripted claim shape --\n#279's `_apply_engine_repoll_backoff` trigger is defined over the\nSAME signal this scenario is built from (`verdict == &quot;no_verdict&quot;`,\n`corroborated: false`, `deltaSize: 0`, two consecutive times on one\ntask), and it fires BEFORE a third such pass can ever reach the\nthree-strike guard's own counter: pass 2 is the first ordinary\nwitness (old counter -&gt; 1), but pass 2 is ALSO the first of what\nbecomes two consecutive re-polls, so the re-poll that would have been\npass 3 instead backs the task off for 600s -- requirement A.3's own\n&quot;a re-poll that triggers a backoff neither increments nor resets the\napproach's stagnation counter&quot; -- and the counter never reaches 3.\ntask 014's own sweep crashed an xdist worker on this exact node before\nthis cure (the module's own `_worker_sup` built `sup` directly rather\nthan through `tests.conftest.make_supervisor`, leaving the backoff's\nreal `asyncio.sleep(600)` unpatched -- `_patch_sleep_for_this_test()`\nnow closes that, matching `tests/test_repoll_backoff.py`'s own\ndocumented reasoning for the same gap).\n\nWhat is left to pin, and what this rewrite asserts instead: the claims\nare still recorded and still uncorroborated every time (task 012's\nletter, unaffected by #279); the OLD three-strike STAGNATION_MESSAGE\nnever appears (superseded, not merely absent by accident); #279's own\nbackoff fires twice (`consecutiveCount` 2 then 3, since the third\nscripted call is ALSO a re-poll on the already-once-backed-off task);\nand the task ends up deferred (`pending`, a `re-poll backoff`\n`deferredReason`) rather than whatever the pre-#279 guard would have\nleft it as.\n</code></pre>\n","status":"passed","flaky":false,"newFailed":false,"newBroken":false,"newPassed":false,"retriesCount":0,"retriesStatusChange":false,"beforeStages":[{"name":"tmp_path_factory","time":{"start":1792071797339,"stop":1792071797339,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"event_loop_policy","time":{"start":1792071797339,"stop":1792071797339,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_isolate_ambient_home_in_process","time":{"start":1792072288980,"stop":1792072288995,"duration":15},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"monkeypatch","time":{"start":1792072288980,"stop":1792072288980,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"n